# What belongs in this repo: source, config and the two instruction files.
# Everything below is either regenerated by a build, downloaded by a package
# manager, produced by running the app, or private to one machine.
#
# Sizes on a working checkout, for context:
#   src-tauri/target/   ~11 GB   cargo build cache
#   node_modules/       ~191 MB  npm install
#   src-tauri/bundled/  ~8.5 MB  binaries staged for the app bundle
#   dist/               ~684 KB  vite build
# None of it is tracked, and none of it ever has been.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- JavaScript
# Unanchored on purpose: transitive deps nest their own node_modules.
node_modules/
/quickwp-manager/dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --------------------------------------------------------------- Rust /Tauri
/quickwp-manager/src-tauri/target/
/quickwp-manager/src-tauri/gen/schemas/
# Staged copies of the edge and CLI binaries, produced by build.sh.
/quickwp-manager/src-tauri/bundled/
# Windows installer toolchain, fetched by `tauri build`.
/quickwp-manager/src-tauri/WixTools/
/quickwp-manager/src-tauri/NSIS/

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This workspace builds three
# binaries (the app, the edge daemon, the CLI), and an application commits
# its lockfile so every machine and CI run resolves the same dependency
# tree. That matters more than usual here: the app verifies every runtime it
# downloads against checksums compiled into it, and an unpinned build is a
# build whose provenance nobody can state.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Secrets
# QuickWP generates a local CA. A private key must never reach a remote.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keychain
*.keychain-db
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Tauri updater signing keys.
*.tauri-key
tauri-private.key

# ------------------------------------------------- Runtime data and app state
# The app's own store lives in ~/Library/Application Support, but these turn
# up in a checkout when the examples or tests are run from here.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite
*.pid
/logs/
/quickwp-manager/logs/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Editor and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Scratch
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.backup
/coverage/
/test-results/
